curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:9:The sequence assumes successful completion of the current A1 blueprint. It does not reteach A1 from the beginning: it immediately retrieves familiar transactions, directions, modals, repair language, and controlled Perfekt, then expands them into connected accounts, reasons, comparisons, polite problem-solving, and routine formal communication.
curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:24:The learner can already handle short supported exchanges involving identity, family, routine, food, housing, directions, transport, health, services, work, leisure, plans, and simple past reference. The following A1 structures are available for recycling rather than reintroduction:
curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:163:- **Deliberately recycled:** fixed-location dative (A1 L20, L24); rooms and furniture (A1 L19–L21); directions (A1 L23); requests and confirmation.
curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:189:- **Deliberately recycled:** all Module 2 language; A1 home, neighbourhood, price, directions, and plan-making language.
curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:444:- **Deliberately recycled:** transport and announcements (A1 L25–L30); `erreichen` (L17); Perfekt (L1, L20–L21); reflexive verbs (L14); times and directions.
curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:509:- **Deliberately recycled:** all Module 6 language; A1 transport, time, directions, hotel, plan-change, and repair language.
curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:803:- **Deliberately recycled:** directions (A1 L23–L24); past narration (L1–L2, L31); `wenn` contrast (L29); weather and outdoor planning (L57).
curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:829:- **Deliberately recycled:** all Module 10 language; A1 neighbourhood, weather, directions, services, plans, and event notices.
curriculum/a2_blueprint.md:989:- **Deliberately recycled:** the complete A2 sequence plus A1 identity, time, transactions, directions, services, repair, and basic Perfekt foundations.
